index=f"""# WOF Depth-Fill Index\n\n> This index replaces the prior shell-pack approach with full start-depth content, data-only YAML sidecars, world-specific press bills, and long-form art direction. It specifies a later-release family of solo/private-co-op text worlds and makes no live MMO claim.\n\n{tbl(['worldId','Pack','Module','Maturity','First four hubs','Five-person instance','Big night','YAML sidecar','Target data counts'],index_rows)}\n\n## Anti-template self-check\n\nAll 112 kit names are unique across the 28 worlds: {', '.join(k for w in WORLDS for k in w['kits'])}. No kit uses the prohibited role labels. Durable NPC lines are world-named and place-specific. Quest titles follow an authored spine rather than a shared eight-noun rotation. Module probes carry given state, action, expected ledger, and forbidden prose fields. Art briefs name actual kits, places, chrome, materials, crops, and safety variants.\n\n## Per-world table counts\n\n{tbl(['worldId','Places','NPCs','Quests','Species','Items','Interactables','Choice buttons'],counts)}\n\n## 30-line integrity checklist\n\n"""+'\n'.join(f"{i+1:02d}. [x] {x}" for i,x in enumerate(checks))+"\n"
